Spec: Process-pinned control client

Purpose:
  Exchange bounded control requests only with the live process selected by a trusted launcher.

Owns:
  ./VerifiedPipeClient.cs

References:
  /contracts/dotnet/LinkGate.Control/FrameCodec.sdd
  /contracts/dotnet/LinkGate.Control/ControlJson.sdd

Must:
  Negotiate connection.api separately and strictly validate correlated formal operation/status replies under the existing unknown-outcome and process-pin boundary.
  Require a live process handle supplied by a trusted launcher; duplicate and hold it for the connection lifetime.
  Accept only local canonical LinkGate control pipe names.
  Before writing, obtain the OS pipe server PID and compare its held process identity and creation time to the pin.
  Fail closed on exited peers, failed native checks, cancellation or mismatched identity; never retry or select another process.
  Bound connect and each exchange to two seconds and serialize exchanges without an unbounded queue.
  Validate strict JSON response, request correlation and exclusive result/error shape before returning a cloned result.
  Dispose owned pipe and process handles on all failed connections and on disposal.
  Require explicit opt-in to experimental pending registration and an application-supplied operation UUID.
  Once a mutation write is attempted, report interrupted or malformed replies as an unknown outcome with the same operation UUID.
  Validate method-specific results and fixed error fields; never expose raw server messages or details.
  Keep public client namespace `LinkGate.Client` and replace only the unpublished development API location.
  Refuse requests beyond the negotiated session request limit before attempting a write.
  Require negotiated `grant.request.pending` and explicit experimental opt-in for pending permission requests, with caller-persisted operation IDs and typed result validation.
  Require negotiated `secure.stream.direct` and explicit experimental opt-in for secure streams; validate connection status and attachment names without retrying mutations.
  Negotiate secure.stream.relay separately before opens and ready attachments; allow retained closed relay outcomes to be queried after restart even when no current relay routes exist.

Must not:
  Treat this pin as installed-binary verification, automatic discovery or same-user malicious-code isolation.
